    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Is $1200$ a term of the sequence $2,\\ 16,\\ 128,\\ldots$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No.",
      "worked": "$a=2$ and $r=8$.\n\nTest if $1200$ is a term:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a_n&=ar^{n-1}\\\\1200&=2(8)^{n-1}\\\\600&=8^{n-1}\\\\\\log_8 600&=n-1\\\\n-1&\\approx3.076\\\\n&\\approx4.076\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $n$ is not a positive integer, $1200$ is not a term of the sequence.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
